## Summary

Implemented the Exercism **grade-school** roster in `grade_school.py`.

**ZERO (COV-3):** Decomposed into add/enroll, per-grade query, and sorted roster. Researched the canonical exercise (exa MCP websearch → Exercism docs/instructions) and read the canonical spec; evaluated two approaches: (a) per-grade dict of unsorted lists sorted lazily on read, (b) keep lists globally sorted on insert. Chose (a) — `dict[int, list[str]]` + lazy `sorted()` — because ordering only matters at read time, inserts stay O(1), and it's the simplest correct structure; rejected (b) as it adds insert-time cost and bookkeeping for no benefit.

**Implementation:** `School` holds `_roster` (grade→names), `_added` (per-call bool history), and `_names` (O(1) global-uniqueness set). `add_student` rejects a name already enrolled in *any* grade (appends `False`) else enrolls and appends `True`; `roster()` sorts grades then names; `grade(n)` returns sorted names or `[]`; `added()` returns a copy.

**Mode:** AUTO · **Verifier:** direct read (non-web) — pure Python class, no UI/HTTP.
**COV-9:** state-skip — workspace is untracked inside the eval framework repo (no standalone git repo) and has no `script/`/runner; documented in `tests/decisions.md`.

